course: dictionary
lesson: 16139
title: Wickedness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wickedness is a noun. It means being very bad, cruel or evil. «The wickedness of the queen made the whole kingdom afraid.» The word names the quality of being wicked, just as kindness names the quality of being kind.
explain: Look at the words around it to find its meaning. In «The stepmother's wickedness made the children cry», the word cry tells you the stepmother was cruel. Try your meaning in the sentence: could you swap in very cruel or very bad and still make sense? If yes, you have it.
explain: In church and Bible lessons, wickedness can also mean sin: doing evil against God and other people. «The prophet spoke out against the wickedness of the people.» Christians believe God forgives those who turn from wickedness.
fact: Wickedness means being very bad, cruel or evil.
fact: Wickedness is uncountable: we do not say "a wickedness" or "wickednesses".
fact: In the Bible, wickedness means sin and doing evil against God and other people.
fact: «Turn from wickedness» means stop doing evil and change your ways.
fact: The adjective is «wicked», as in «the wicked witch».
exercise: «The wickedness of the stepmother made the children cry.» What does wickedness mean here? | Being very kind and generous | Being very clean and tidy | Being very tired after a long day | *Being very cruel and bad
exercise: «The witch's wickedness was punished at last.» Find and copy one word that tells you what happened to the wickedness. | witch's | was | *punished | last
exercise: In the Bible, what does wickedness mean? | A kind gift for a friend | A type of bread baked at Easter | Being very tall for your age | *Sin, and doing evil against God and other people
test: Can you say "a wickedness" or "wickednesses"? | Yes, both are correct | *No, wickedness is uncountable, so it has no plural | Yes, but only in the plural
test: Which word is the adjective from the same family as wickedness? | wickedness | wicker | wickedly | *wicked
exam: Pick the sentence where wickedness is used correctly. | *The villain's wickedness frightened the whole village | The kind nurse showed great wickedness to her patients | Wickedness is the loud noise the dog made | We ate wickedness for lunch
